The event wait in every process. NullMoth's own change (not an upstream Mesa commit).
Waits on GPU work (vkWaitForFences, the channel's own waits) poll their first millisecond as before, then sleep in
the NVRM kext on the device's graphics completion event instead of polling (a thread whose waits run past 2 ms
sleeps after a 50 us spin); WindowServer keeps the eager sleep it had. The rules are in nvkmd/nvrm/nvrm_evwait.h,
a byte-for-byte copy of kexts/NVRM/nvrm_evwait.h
(tools/test_shared_headers.py compares them; tools/test_evwait_policy.c and tools/test_evwait_loop.c test them).
NVRM_EVENT_WAIT=0 in /Library/GPUBundles/nvmtl/nvrm610.conf turns the sleep off (polling as before).

